    <p class="jump-nav__label">Jump to section</p>
    <ul class="jump-nav__list">
      <li><a href="#verdict">The verdict</a></li>
      <li><a href="#evidence">What the data shows</a></li>
      <li><a href="#routes">Routes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sales">Who pays you</a></li>
      <li><a href="#ai">AI and disruption</a></li>
      <li><a href="#better">Better alternatives</a></li>
      <li><a href="#learn">Learn it cheaply</a></li>
      <li><a href="#role">Accounting, FP&A and busin</a></li>
      <li><a href="#meeting">A monthly business review </a></li>
      <li><a href="#money">Money</a></li>
      <li><a href="#checkpoint">The 4-Checkpoint Protocol</a></li>
      <li><a href="#gate3">The 3 Gates</a></li>
      <li><a href="#mistakes">Expensive mistakes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#next-step">What to do next</a></li>
      <li><a href="#faq">FAQs</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <h2 id="verdict">The verdict: bridge finance and operations and show business impact</h2>

  <p>
    Prepare in stages and keep proof. Employers and clients look for evidence, not claims.
  </p>
  <p>
    Check what your target role actually asks for by reading notices, then practise that version of the skill.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Type of graduate</th>
          <th>Our read</th>
          <th>Why</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Type of graduate"><strong>Recommendations backed by simple models</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Our read">Strong</td>
          <td data-label="Why">Leaders act on clarity.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Type of graduate"><strong>Understanding the supported team</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Our read">Strong</td>
          <td data-label="Why">Advice must fit reality.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Type of graduate"><strong>Moving from FP&A to partnering</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Our read">Good</td>
          <td data-label="Why">It is a common path.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Type of graduate"><strong>Pure reporting with no advice</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Our read">Risky</td>
          <td data-label="Why">Automation puts it under pressure.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="evidence">What can be said with confidence, and what cannot</h2>

  <p>
    Read ten notices for finance business partner roles and write one recommendation note.
  </p>
  <p>
    We could not confirm how every employer or client assesses this. Ask two people in your target field.
  </p>
  <p>
    See also <a href="/blog/career-options/career-in-finance-vs-accounting-india/">finance vs accounting careers</a> and <a href="/blog/career-options/mba-finance-career-paths-banking-and-corporate-finance-india/">MBA finance career paths</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="note-line">
    We did not rely on statistics for this page. The notices, conversations and your projects are the evidence.
  </p>
  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      Practice is free. Use the 10% rule of thumb for any paid course, with 20% as a caution, as an illustration, not a real fee.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="routes">Seven routes, strongest growth first</h2>

  <div class="route-grid">
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">01</span>
        <span class="chip chip--high">Scalable</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Independent finance advisory for small firms</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Serve owners who need numbers explained.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Small firms.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Two client cases.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Needs trust and rules compliance.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Add retainers.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">02</span>
        <span class="chip chip--high">Scalable</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Finance business partner in a company</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Support a business team.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Employers.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Decision cases.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Needs credibility with teams.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Move toward finance head.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">03</span>
        <span class="chip chip--mid">Scalable with a business layer</span>
      </div>
      <h3>FP&A analyst</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Budget, forecast and report.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Employers.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>A model.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Deadline pressure.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Move toward partner roles.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">04</span>
        <span class="chip chip--mid">Scalable with a business layer</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Accounting and controllership</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Keep books and controls.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Employers.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Clean audits.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Rule-heavy.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Move toward controller.</p>
